[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186129412 :question/answer-fields 17592186125972] {:db/id 17592186129217 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-325cb3ef-db56-5f90-98ae-212e45702d0f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-325cb3ef-db56-5f90-98ae-212e45702d0f" :question/id #uuid "325cb3ef-db56-5f90-98ae-212e45702d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-109145" :question/problem "Consider the arc of the curve $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ that lies between $y=0$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${y}_{1}=0$ to ${y}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64fdecf4-7be9-5050-b772-01b00e36fa6a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64fdecf4-7be9-5050-b772-01b00e36fa6a" :answer-field/id #uuid "64fdecf4-7be9-5050-b772-01b00e36fa6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d151476d-b4bb-5405-af19-fe054e71c98a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5126c3d8-978f-582d-85b3-1b273093c176" "answer-8ba1a2b2-1160-53df-9d34-b83861b916c1" "answer-d151476d-b4bb-5405-af19-fe054e71c98a" "answer-b59b2a2c-fb0b-5db0-9b18-977f28ffedf9" "answer-d70bd935-3591-5e22-b322-ce29e2d33415"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5126c3d8-978f-582d-85b3-1b273093c176" :answer/id #uuid "5126c3d8-978f-582d-85b3-1b273093c176" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ba1a2b2-1160-53df-9d34-b83861b916c1" :answer/id #uuid "8ba1a2b2-1160-53df-9d34-b83861b916c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d151476d-b4bb-5405-af19-fe054e71c98a" :answer/id #uuid "d151476d-b4bb-5405-af19-fe054e71c98a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b59b2a2c-fb0b-5db0-9b18-977f28ffedf9" :answer/id #uuid "b59b2a2c-fb0b-5db0-9b18-977f28ffedf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}y\\sqrt{1+{sec}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d70bd935-3591-5e22-b322-ce29e2d33415" :answer/id #uuid "d70bd935-3591-5e22-b322-ce29e2d33415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}y\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129216 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cbe7ea72-e04a-55e6-a4f7-365b15606888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cbe7ea72-e04a-55e6-a4f7-365b15606888" :question/id #uuid "cbe7ea72-e04a-55e6-a4f7-365b15606888" :question/math-academy-id "q-109257" :question/problem "Consider the arc of the curve $y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}$ that lies between the lines $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ Calculate the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${x}_{1}=-1$ to ${x}_{2}=1.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,⇒\\,{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\pi x\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\pi [1-(-1)] \\\\  & =8\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54638d73-c9f4-5d31-93a7-16d80e13c507"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54638d73-c9f4-5d31-93a7-16d80e13c507" :answer-field/id #uuid "54638d73-c9f4-5d31-93a7-16d80e13c507" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bacbe449-5ccd-5971-8f8e-92d50f996dba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3e914b0d-41ca-50e1-920b-daa562691bf8" "answer-d807f0fc-fb4a-570e-8af5-96a9583d0e92" "answer-bacbe449-5ccd-5971-8